From: RE-CS-06 minimal build
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: re-cs-06: explicitly initialize USB clock rates

The stock-loader unit leaves AUX, LFPS and mock UTMI at the 24 MHz XO
reset rate. The same r14 on the modified-loader unit has 2 MHz AUX,
25 MHz LFPS and 60 MHz mock UTMI and enumerates the same bridge at USB3.
Request the board's GCC-supported rates before the USB wrapper probes,
so DWC3 derives reference timing from the configured clock, not inherited
bootloader state. No live controller rebinding or bootloader replacement.
The kernel-only test restored 5G/UAS on the stock-loader unit, including an
owner-confirmed power cycle. Device/power/hotplug coverage remains limited.

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5322-re-cs-06.dts b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5322-re-cs-06.dts
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5322-re-cs-06.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5322-re-cs-06.dts
@@ -152,6 +152,12 @@
 		 <&gcc GCC_USB0_AUX_CLK>,
 		 <&gcc GCC_USB0_LFPS_CLK>;
 	clock-names = "core", "sleep", "mock_utmi", "aux", "lfps";
+	/* Do not inherit USB reference/timing rates from the bootloader. */
+	assigned-clocks = <&gcc GCC_USB0_MASTER_CLK>,
+			  <&gcc GCC_USB0_MOCK_UTMI_CLK>,
+			  <&gcc GCC_USB0_AUX_CLK>,
+			  <&gcc GCC_USB0_LFPS_CLK>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <200000000>, <60000000>, <2000000>, <25000000>;
 
 	/delete-property/ qcom,select-utmi-as-pipe-clk;
 };
